
==========================================================================
  QS_3 dummy-register simulator  (P_3 = ℂ[S_3] control, log-tree dispatch)
==========================================================================

  Control    P_3 = ℂ[S_3]   arity-8 padded datatype, 3 tag qubits
             (6 real S_3 slots + 2 |id⟩ duplicates for power-of-2 arity)
  Regs       T ⊗ D_1 ⊗ D_2 ⊗ D_3   4 qubits
  Total      3 + 4 = 7 qubits

  Six permutations of S_3 each occupy one summand:
    id      : π = (1, 2, 3)    swap_23 : π = (1, 3, 2)
    swap_12 : π = (2, 1, 3)    cyc_123 : π = (2, 3, 1)
    swap_13 : π = (3, 2, 1)    cyc_132 : π = (3, 1, 2)

  R_k(π)  = coherent SWAP(T, D_{π(k)}) via `control` on S_3
           (dispatch via log-depth binary tree over 3 tag qubits)
  F       = id_T ⊗ X on D_1 ⊗ H on D_2 ⊗ Z on D_3   (F² = I)
  round_k = R_k ; (id_S3 ⊗ F) ; R_k                 (round_k² = id)
  qs3_sim = round_1 ; round_2 ; round_3            (n = 3 rounds)

  Total oracle calls: n² = 9  (each f_i applied n = 3 times).
  Total circuit depth (algorithmic): n·log n = 3·log 6 ≈ 8.

